    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0d4ffc0e-72d4-5ca1-bcf2-e4b8c96adefa",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Susan, the new receptionist of the Smithsonian Museum in Washington DC, uses the following three functions to model the daily number of visitors to the museum $t$ minutes after the museum has opened.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of people inside the museum\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which people enter the museum\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which people leave the museum\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of people inside the museum $t$ minutes after opening. Then,\n\n$$\nN'(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}N(t)}{\\textrm{d}t} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Change in }N}{\\textrm{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, $N'(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of people inside the museum changes $t$ minutes after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of people inside the museum at time $t$ by finding the difference between the entry and exit rates at time $t.$ That is,\n\n$$\nN'(t) = E(t) - L(t).\n$$\n\nThe change ratio denotes an instantaneous rate: the limit of change ratios as the time interval tends to zero.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4489857c-bae8-599e-b263-21807b819311",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "2e2cd18a-32da-50aa-ae8f-473135719e07",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "N^{′}(t) = E(t) \\cdot L(t)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "101159f6-c7e1-587c-b735-e9a911f83175",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "N(t) = E(t) + L(t)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "44a80694-19e0-580b-815f-c40e4608fb0d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "N^{′}(t) = E(t) - L(t)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "579b0574-8d71-561e-99fd-82f754ed5fa8",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "N(t) = E(t) - L(t)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "978bdd27-9034-531d-b183-05146d928957",
